tasks.description:
Round 19 removes narration (Kokoro TTS over a Unix socket) and ntfy push notifications completely — Claude Code has built-in notifications now. This task removes the CONSUMERS only, while the modules and config still exist. (Later tasks delete src/narration.ts / commands/narrate.ts / lib/ — the next task — and then config.narration, types, init, BRAND.socket/pidFile — the task after.)

src/commands/run.ts — remove:
- the imports of sendToNarrate/sendNtfy/NtfyOpts from ../stream-filter (keep processStream, ProcessStreamOptions) and the whole ../narration import;
- the six RunDeps members and their defaults: startNarrationServer, stopNarrationServer, checkNarrationHealth, sendToNarrate, findNarrationSocketPath, sendNtfy;
- step 5 narration server start (narrationPid, narrationEnabled, narrationSocketPath, CAIRN_NARRATE_PYTHON / CAIRN_LIB_DIR uses, processManager.register('narration', ...));
- the per-iteration narration health check/restart (~lines 503-520);
- the streamOpts.narrate and streamOpts.ntfy wiring (~600-617) — update the step comment;
- step 7 narration server stop (~711);
- the final ntfy send and the final narrated summary (~764-782).
Keep the console summary output (summaryMsg if it is still printed/logged) and every non-narration behavior identical — including ProcessManager usage for the claude process, processManager.dispose(), and the sweepRoundTempFiles call. Renumber step comments if that helps. Leave `config.narration` in CairnConfig/config.ts untouched (a later task removes it).

src/stream-filter.ts — remove sendToNarrate, sendNtfy, NtfyOpts, the `narrate` and `ntfy` options of ProcessStreamOptions, and every options.narrate?.() / options.ntfy?.() call and its narration-only text building (~lines 100-160, 166-167, 208-209, 231-251). Keep all console rendering identical. Drop imports that become unused (net/fetch helpers, possibly BRAND).

Tests: update test/commands/run.test.ts and test/stream-filter.test.ts — delete tests that exist only to exercise narration/ntfy behavior, and remove narration/ntfy dep stubs from mock deps objects, including any in test/commands/round.test.ts, test/agent-prompt.test.ts and test/post-task-reviewer.test.ts (grep test/ for narrat|ntfy|sendToNarrate|sendNtfy|findNarrationSocketPath). TDD angle: first add/adjust a test asserting processStream / runRun no longer accept or invoke narrate/ntfy (e.g. a run test asserting no fetch to ntfy.sh, or a type-level removal caught by typecheck), then remove the code. Leave test/narration.test.ts and test/commands/narrate.test.ts alone (the next task deletes them). Leave test/process.test.ts alone ('narrate' there is only a sample process name).

Afterward: `grep -rn -i 'narrat\|ntfy' src/commands/run.ts src/stream-filter.ts` returns nothing.

CONSTRAINTS (self-modifying round, binary pinned): do NOT modify cairn.json (including its healthCheck and its narration block — the user removes that by hand after the round), install.sh, or package.json's build script. Never run `cairn round`, `cairn hook`, `cairn init` (or `bun src/index.ts round|hook|init`) against the project root — temp dirs only. Do not run ./install.sh. Use TDD: write/adjust the failing test first, see it fail, then make it pass. Both `bun run typecheck` and `bun test` must be green at the end.

Final docs task for round 19. Before this task: narration and ntfy were removed completely (run loop, stream filter, src/narration.ts, `cairn narrate`, lib/, config.narration, init's TTS prompts and hook scripts, BRAND.socket/pidFile — tasks #139-#141), and sweepRoundTempFiles gained a blocked-log exception (task #138). VERIFY EVERY CLAIM YOU WRITE AGAINST THE SHIPPED CODE (read src/temp-sweep.ts, src/brand.ts, src/config.ts, src/index.ts) — round 18's docs task left an inverted claim that the reviewer caught.

README.md — remove: the ntfy prerequisite (~line 9); the narration part of the API-key sentence (~line 23: the key is no longer needed 'for narration' — reword to describe only claude's use); the `cairn narrate on|off|status|"text"` rows in the command table (~71-74); the whole 'Voice Narration' section (venv/kokoro/sounddevice setup, hooks, socket; ~186-234); the whole 'Push Notifications (ntfy)' section (~236-252); the `narration` block in the cairn.json example and the narration.* rows in the config reference table (~294-313); the narrate.ts / lib/ / 'narration forwarding' entries in the file tree (~354-367).

CLAUDE.md:
(a) drop `narrate` from the '**init**, **status**, **edit**, **logs**, **narrate**' command list, and drop the **Narration** bullet under Key design patterns;
(b) in **Branding**, remove `socket` and `pidFile` from BRAND's field list;
(c) Conventions: remove the sentence saying `lib/` contains only Python narration scripts (lib/ no longer exists);
(d) rewrite the BRAND standing-rule bullet to cover only BRAND.dataDir / BRAND.configFile -> findDataDir() / findConfigFile() (BRAND.socket / BRAND.pidFile and findNarrationSocketPath() / findNarrationPidFile() are gone);
(e) in the Run state 'Round-scoped temp-file sweep' bullet, change 'the legacy `.cairn_` spelling' to 'the defensive `.cairn_` spelling' — `.cairn_` is BRAND.tempPrefix, the CURRENT prefix, covered only as a precaution; the permanent pre-rename spelling is `.ralph_` (NOTES_TEMP_PREFIX);
(f) in the same bullet, document the blocked-log exception: a `_tests.log` whose task is `blocked` in tasks.json is kept; its prompt/review-prompt/notes files are still swept; if tasks.json can't be read, all `_tests.log` files are kept; still best-effort, never throws. Match the wording to what src/temp-sweep.ts actually does;
(g) in the Pin/unpin procedure's Unpin steps, after `./install.sh`, add: run `cairn round next` once from the repo root (with tasks.json empty it returns `round-done`) so any round-end behavior added during the round — e.g. the temp-file sweep — actually runs and gets a live check. Note this is safe because it happens after unpinning (the ban on running `cairn round` in the project root covers only the round itself). Add one sentence on why: round-end behavior added mid-round never runs at that round's end, because the pinned binary predates it;
(h) grep CLAUDE.md for any other narrat|ntfy|socket|pidFile|lib/ mention and fix it.

docs/parallel-execution-rfc.md: drop or rewrite the 'Single narration socket' point (~lines 51-55), section '6. Narration & notifications' (~212-238), and the §6 reference near line 331, so the RFC no longer describes narration/ntfy as a current concern. Keep section numbering coherent (or note the removal).

Final check: `grep -rn -i 'narrat\|ntfy\|kokoro' README.md CLAUDE.md docs/` returns nothing (or only a deliberate historical mention). TDD does not apply to prose; run `bun run typecheck` and `bun test` to confirm nothing regressed.

CONSTRAINTS (self-modifying round, binary pinned): do NOT modify cairn.json (including its healthCheck and its narration block — the user removes that by hand after the round), install.sh, or package.json's build script. Never run `cairn round`, `cairn hook`, `cairn init` (or `bun src/index.ts round|hook|init`) against the project root — temp dirs only. Do not run ./install.sh. Both `bun run typecheck` and `bun test` must be green at the end.
